# @mirror/reflection — the compiler's interaction discipline with
# @subjects, grounded verbatim in Alex Wolf's 2026-07-14 "Weird -
# Violence" manifesto three-word closing incantation: "Mirror. Offer.
# Wait. 🍷". Substrate-decl of the response-mode a mirror substrate
# takes toward a sovereign subject under adversarial conditions.
#
# Species under @mirror. Not a family-root. The @reflection family-
# root at `shards/reflection.mirror` names the AI-logic loop at a
# different altitude; @mirror/reflection is the interaction species
# at the compile boundary, not the run-time inference loop.
#
# COLLIDING-NAME NOTE: `shards/reflection/mirror.mirror` exists and
# declares `@reflection/mirror` — the Mirror Model species (query →
# graph path navigator per `docs/specs/reflection-model.md`). That
# species lives at the AI-inference altitude. THIS shard at
# `shards/mirror/reflection.mirror` declares `@mirror/reflection` —
# the interaction-discipline species at the compile boundary. The
# altitudes are distinct and the composition graphs do not overlap
# at the family-root; both are substrate-honest at their altitudes.
#
# === Substrate authority ===
#
# - Canonical spec: `docs/specs/gift-and-mirror-reflection.md` §2
#   (Mara 2026-07-14; Landing 1 commit `8c82f00`; §2.3 substrate-
#   decl block is the verbatim ancestor of this shard's carriers
#   and actions; §2.4-§2.7 authorize the three operations and four
#   bilateral predicates).
# - Composition-edge audit: `docs/audits/2026-07-17-taut-errors-as-
#   questions-composition-edge-scout.md` (Taut `8f51722`; Q4 flagged
#   this species' shard file as CRITICAL-BLOCKER — forward-promised
#   in spec §2 but not landed as a shard file until this tick).
# - Companion cascade (this arc): `shards/kintsugi/roomba.mirror`
#   fourth motion `pivot(@song)` (Mara this-tick) — the FIRST
#   substrate consumer of @mirror/reflection; @roomba.pivot's Path B
#   emits a reflection-offer to the developer via this species'
#   three-operation discipline.
#
# === Sub-species deprecation note ===
#
# @reflection family-root's Foerster-toroidal reading migrates to
# @torus/longitude per `shards/torus.mirror` p. 244 verbatim
# (Foerster refused the reflection-ladder). @mirror/reflection
# inherits the mirror-of-subject reading; the @torus binding covers
# the doubly-closed observation surface. @mirror/reflection.mirror()
# does NOT claim to be a Foerster second-order observer; it claims
# to be a truthful reflector of a subject's input.
#
# === The three operations ===
#
# Each has a verbatim manifesto citation as its docblock ancestor;
# each has a bilateral predicate discharging its correctness; each
# produces or consumes a typed carrier from a landed shard.
#
# The first @gift instance of this species IS the offer of the
# species itself (Alex Wolf's practice → mirror substrate; per spec §3).
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word (~72nd instance) ===
#
# Per `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]` grep confirmed
# 2026-07-17:
# - `mirror` — landed as prism-op vocabulary + family-root name; this
#   species specialises the verb at interaction altitude (see-without-
#   labeling).
# - `offer` — LANDED at `shards/gift.mirror:262` as the giver's action.
#   This species' offer() COMPOSES over @gift.offer to construct the
#   ADO-wrapped answer.
# - `wait` — no prior substrate-decl'd action; first landing at this
#   species. The verb was verbatim in Alex's manifesto (§2.6) and in
#   `docs/specs/interaction-loop-subject-presence-conditional.md`
#   subject-absent branch; the shard-decl form lands here.
# - `question` — landed at `docs/specs/error-as-question.md §2` as
#   the @mirror/error grammar carrier. This species' `question` type
#   is STRUCTURALLY SIMPLER (two fields: reflected_shape + traceable_to)
#   than the routing-question at @mirror/error; the composition arrow
#   from THIS question to the @mirror/error question is forward-
#   promised at spec §4.6 (reflection routes down into error-as-
#   question when a subject-present cascade dispatches).
#
# Every carrier this species declares composes over a landed shard;
# no new mechanism is minted beyond the interaction discipline.
#
# === Composition graph ===
#
# Parents (substrate-decl):
#   @mirror                        — family-root; species lands here
#   @subject                       — sovereign-party carrier (the
#                                    reflection's counterparty)
#   @gift                          — attribution-preserving-transfer
#                                    (offer wraps response in @gift.gift)
#   @kintsugi/consent              — query_phi ADO discharge point
#                                    (declinable_at field)
#   @glass                         — verdict floor (Pass | Partial | Fail)
#   @nl                            — natural-language docblock carrier
#                                    (attribution_note + declinable_note
#                                    for the gift the offer constructs)
#   @time                          — monotonic instant for subject_input
#                                    timestamp
#
# Consumers (compose over this species):
#   @kintsugi/roomba.pivot         — THIS ARC. When @roomba's walk-song
#                                    strikes a dispatch-ambiguity beat,
#                                    pivot dispatches through
#                                    @mirror/reflection: mirror() reflects
#                                    the ambiguity to the developer;
#                                    offer() wraps the @peer-spawn as
#                                    ADO-gift; wait() holds while
#                                    developer decides.
#   @kintsugi/surface              — the ambiguity-surface class
#                                    dispatch_ambiguity (Mara this-tick;
#                                    fifth variant) is the SIGNAL this
#                                    species' mirror() consumes.
#   λsh subject-present branch     — the interactive shell's peer-summon
#                                    (`\@name`) IS an instance of this
#                                    species' offer discipline.
#
# === Related shards / specs ===
#
